<title>UK: ABN AMRO London wins April Reuter forex poll.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO London wins April Reuter forex poll.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABN AMRO in London has won the April Reuter foreign exchange poll, beating other banks and financial institutions from across the globe.</p>
<p>The ABN AMRO forecasts gave them an average divergence from the actual rates of 0.9702 percent.</p>
<p>UBS in London came second with 0.9904 percent, followed by NatWest Markets, London in third place with a 1.2939 percent divergence rate.</p>
<p>The average divergence rates of the 34 institutions who participated varied between 0.9702 and 5.0620 percent.</p>
<p>The rankings were based on the accuracy of the one-month forecast against the April 30 European closing mid-rates of dollar/mark at 1.7215, dollar/yen at 126.95 and sterling/dollar at $1.6206.</p>
